307:                 "summary": "Webhook Subscribe",
308:                 "description": "Subscribe: get every new mail pushed to your endpoint, the moment it arrives.\n\nOne endpoint per team. A second call replaces the URL and the secret. The answer holds\nthe signing `secret`. **It is shown only here, keep it.**\n\n**What we send.** One `POST` per mail that arrives in your mailbox after this call\n(older mail is not pushed):\n\n```json\n{\"event\": \"mail.received\", \"message\": { ...the same object as a poll item... }}\n```\n\nHeaders: `X-Webhook-Event`, `X-Webhook-Id` (the mail id), `X-Webhook-Timestamp`\n(Unix seconds) and `X-Webhook-Signature`.\n\n**Check the signature** before you trust a call. It is\n`sha256=` + hex HMAC-SHA256, key = your secret, message = timestamp + `.` + raw body:\n\n```python\nexpected = \"sha256=\" + hmac.new(\n    secret.encode(), timestamp.encode() + b\".\" + raw_body, hashlib.sha256\n).hexdigest()\nok = hmac.compare_digest(expected, signature_header)\n```\n\nDo not accept a call with a wrong signature or a timestamp older than a few minutes.\n\n**Rules.**\n- Answer with any 2xx within 5 seconds. Do your work after you answered.\n- No 2xx: we try 3 times in about 15 seconds, then drop that push. Nothing is lost: the\n  mail is still in `GET /v1/mailbox/messages`. Keep a slow poll as your safety net.\n- A push can arrive twice or out of order. Use `message.id` to skip repeats.\n- The URL must be public (a tunnel to your laptop is fine). Redirects are not followed.\n- Attachments are listed, not sent: download them as usual.\n- A new team key removes the subscription. Subscribe again with the new key.\n- Limits may be tuned.\n\nTry it with `POST /v1/mailbox/webhook/test`.",
